Manage custom evaluators.

Usage
  azd ai eval evaluator [command]

Available Commands
  create   : Register an evaluator, publishing its first version.
  delete   : Delete an evaluator version.
  download : Download a registered evaluator version's definition.
  list     : List the project's evaluators, or the built-in ones.
  show     : Show an evaluator definition.
  update   : Publish a new version of an evaluator.
  versions : Inspect the versions of one evaluator.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for evaluator
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Discover built-in evaluators
    azd ai eval evaluator list --builtin

Use azd ai eval evaluator [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
